WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.648
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Tuesday, November third.

2
00:00:04.648 --> 00:00:12.449
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.449 --> 00:00:15.161
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.161 --> 00:00:28.723
Today: U.S. strikes on Iran's Qeshm Island, new Houthi drone claims against Saudi airports, Houthi forces nearing Aden, attacks on Pakistan's polio campaign, and the abduction of Islamic school students in Nigeria.

5
00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:30.214
We start in Iran.

6
00:00:30.214 --> 00:00:39.882
Reuters reports, citing U.S. officials, that the United States carried out what officials called defensive strikes on Iran's Qeshm Island in the Strait of Hormuz.

7
00:00:39.882 --> 00:00:48.982
Radio Free Europe reports the strike happened yesterday and is the latest in a series of previously undisclosed U.S. military operations against Iran.

8
00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.855
Turning to Saudi Arabia.

9
00:00:50.855 --> 00:00:51.584
The U.S.

10
00:00:51.584 --> 00:01:04.985
State Department says Iranian-supported Houthis have attacked civilian airports and other critical infrastructure in Saudi Arabia, causing civilian casualties and severe travel disruptions, and that the hostilities could escalate rapidly.

11
00:01:04.985 --> 00:01:13.307
It warns of possible airport attacks, airspace closures and flight cancellations, and urges extreme caution at Saudi airports.

12
00:01:13.307 --> 00:01:25.207
Separately, Houthi military spokesman Yahya Sarea claimed drone strikes over the past forty eight hours on King Fahd International Airport in Dammam and on a radar site and the airport in Jazan, according to reports citing Reuters.

13
00:01:25.207 --> 00:01:31.605
Australia continues to advise do not travel to Saudi Arabia.

14
00:01:31.605 --> 00:01:33.193
An update on Yemen.

15
00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:39.590
Reuters reports, citing sources, that Houthi forces have advanced to within eighty kilometers of Aden.

16
00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:40.465
Next, Pakistan.

17
00:01:40.465 --> 00:01:51.752
The Pakistani broadcaster Hum News reports two police officers guarding an anti-polio vaccination team were killed and another was injured in a shooting in Mohmand district, in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, this morning.

18
00:01:51.752 --> 00:01:54.359
Pakistan's president condemned the attack.

19
00:01:54.359 --> 00:02:07.270
Separately, The Thursday Times reports police said gunmen fired on a polio team and abducted four workers in Tank district yesterday, as a week-long drive to vaccinate about twenty four million children began.

20
00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.340
And in Nigeria.

21
00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:25.811
Channels Television and The Cable report gunmen suspected to be bandits abducted fourteen Islamic school students and their teacher on Saturday, October thirty first, while they were harvesting maize on the teacher's farm in Tungan Bako village, near Pandogari, in Rafi local government area of Niger State.

22
00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:28.951
Niger State police confirmed the abduction.

23
00:02:28.951 --> 00:02:31.751
Now a few quick notes by region.

24
00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.982
In Asia, an update on India.

25
00:02:33.982 --> 00:02:43.490
Reuters reports Cyclone Murasu made landfall on India's eastern coast, the second storm to hit the region in a week, and Canada says it is tracking the storm in Andhra Pradesh.

26
00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:59.435
Reuters also reports North Korea tested a strategic cruise missile with a dispersal warhead, according to state media, and that an Indian national was killed and a New Zealander injured when two helicopters collided in Nepal's Mount Everest region.

27
00:02:59.435 --> 00:03:09.625
In Europe, Reuters reports NATO will deploy maritime patrol aircraft, radars and drones to the Black Sea after seven strikes on cargo ships near Romania and Bulgaria last month.

28
00:03:09.625 --> 00:03:10.507
The U.K.

29
00:03:10.507 --> 00:03:18.267
Foreign Office updated its Greece travel advice with new information on winter weather, including flash flooding.

30
00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:30.456
In Africa, Congolese outlets including Le Potentiel report nearly fifty people held by the A D F armed group were freed in the Malembi forest in Ituri province, and twenty nine have been returned to their families in Mambasa.

31
00:03:30.456 --> 00:03:43.374
And in cyber, Britain's National Cyber Security Centre warned the country should be prepared for an A I powered cyberattack on critical infrastructure within two years, according to Reuters.

32
00:03:43.374 --> 00:03:56.451
The Record reports supermarket refrigerators across Europe appear to have been hacked again, the second such wave in recent weeks, and that hackers claimed to have taken down Russia's federal statistics agency, Rosstat.

33
00:03:56.451 --> 00:04:05.260
The Record also reports the F B I and Secret Service attributed the six point three billion dollar theft from the crypto platform Binance to a North Korean hacking group.

34
00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.272
That's today's brief.

35
00:04:07.272 --> 00:04:16.944
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

36
00:04:16.944 --> 00:04:25.273
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

37
00:04:25.273 --> 00:04:27.413
This brief is digitally narrated.

38
00:04:27.413 --> 00:04:28.393
Questions?

39
00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:31.862
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

40
00:04:31.862 --> 00:04:34.079
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
